        "Jacques F. A. P. Miller",
        "Max D. Cooper"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The distinction of B- and T-lymphocyte lineages created a foundational framework for adaptive immunity.",
        "attribution": "Miller and Cooper are a compact and well-defined pairing for the complementary lymphocyte-lineage discoveries.",
        "maturity": "The discoveries have been confirmed and elaborated across modern immunology for many decades.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Its age and broad conceptual nature require comparison with discoveries that have a more direct recent clinical consequence."
        ]
      }
    },
