      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Long-term potentiation supplied a durable experimental framework for activity-dependent synaptic change and mechanisms relevant to memory.",
        "attribution": "Lømo and Bliss are central to the original phenomenon, while Morris represents influential work connecting it to learning and memory.",
        "maturity": "The phenomenon and many molecular features are mature, with sustained influence across neuroscience.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Whether long-term potentiation constitutes the synaptic basis of memory in a sufficiently direct causal sense remains debated.",
